{
  "dom_id": "step-e10072",
  "name": "Example: Translating Contextual Problems Into Differential Equations",
  "problem": "Since the year $2000$, a herd of antelopes multiplies at a rate proportional to their population. Also, the number of antelopes in the herd decreases by $20$ antelopes per year due to predators. What differential equation describes the rate of change in the population of antelopes at time $t,$ where $t$ is the time (in years) since the year $2000?$",
  "worked_solution": "The rate of change in the number of antelopes per year increases in proportion to $P$ and decreases by $20.$ The differential equation that describes this is\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}P}{\\textrm{d}t}=kP - 20,\n$$\n\nwhere $k$ is a (positive) constant of proportionality.",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
